<title>LEBANON: Most Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>Most Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its January 9 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.75 (13.78)	     14.24 (14.27)</p>
<p>    Six months	    14.89 (14.93)	     16.08 (16.13)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.46 (14.46)	     16.90 (16.90)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 19.02 (19.28)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 345740 345723</p>
